    <summary>Windows Explorer thumbnails for 315 file formats, plus a right-click image toolkit.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[Thumbwright is a Windows Explorer thumbnail provider and context-menu toolkit written in Rust.

## Features

- **Thumbnails for 315 formats**: camera RAW (CR3, CR2, CRW, NEF, ARW, ORF, RW2, RAF, X3F, DNG and more), JPEG XL, JPEG 2000, HEIC/AVIF, Blender, Aseprite, GIMP XCF, PSD, Krita, SVG, DWG/DXF, FreeCAD, 3MF, G-code, PDF, EPUB, legacy Office, DjVu, ZIP/7z/RAR and CBZ/CBR comics, video frames, album art, Android APK icons and a long tail of scientific and legacy bitmaps.
- **Right-click toolkit** in both the classic and the Windows 11 menu: convert, resize, lossless JPEG rotation, shrink for email, compress to size, OCR, combine into PDF or CBZ, rename by date or camera, sort into folders, wallpaper, lock screen and folder icon.
- **Isolated decoders**: OS codecs and complex decoders run in a separate process limited by a Job Object (memory, CPU time, no UI access), so a malformed file cannot crash Explorer.
- **Reversible registration**: Thumbwright never changes an extension's existing ProgID or default handler, and uninstall removes exactly what it wrote.
- Command-line tool `twctl` for every menu verb plus batch conversion and diagnostics (`twctl doctor`).

## Notes

- Installs per-machine to `Program Files\Thumbwright` (requires administrator).
- HEIC and AVIF thumbnails use Microsoft's HEIF, HEVC and AV1 codec extensions from the Microsoft Store.
- Windows 11 may keep a newly installed menu entry hidden until you enable it in **Show more options > Customize menu**.
- The Windows 11 menu entry appears after your next sign-in.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/DailenG/Thumbwright/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md</releaseNotes>
